            <ArticleTitle>The &quot;two week syndrome&quot; associated with injection treatment for chronic pain--fact or fiction?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>165-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Many patients attending the pain clinic for regular injections of local anaesthetic state that the pain returned &quot;two weeks&quot; ago. This study demonstrates that 85% of these patients have a &quot;return of pain&quot; interval which coincides with the proximity of their next clinic appointment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
